---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { WHATSAPP_URL } from '../consts';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'AboutPage',
  name: 'About Balli Balli Seoul',
  url: 'https://balliballi.com/about/',
  mainEntity: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'Balli Balli Seoul',
    legalName: '지인어스 (Jiinus)',
    url: 'https://balliballi.com/',
    logo: 'https://balliballi.com/favicon.svg',
    founder: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Yeonbum Kim' },
    areaServed: { '@type': 'City', name: 'Seoul' },
    contactPoint: {
      '@type': 'ContactPoint',
      contactType: 'customer service',
      url: 'https://wa.me/821075191282',
      availableLanguage: ['English', 'Korean'],
    },
    taxID: '108-24-44405',
  },
};
---

<Base
  title="About Us — Balli Balli Seoul"
  description="We run coliving houses in Seoul, and helping our foreign residents with life's breakdowns became a service. Here's who we are and how it works."
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />

  <article class="about">
    <h1>We started this because our housemates kept knocking</h1>

    <p>
      Balli Balli Seoul grew out of something very concrete: <strong>we run
      coliving houses in Seoul</strong>, shared homes where foreign residents
      and students live. When you live under the same roof as people new to
      Korea, you become the default fixer — the person they find when the
      drain clogs, the checkout page won't take a foreign card, or something
      needs cleaning, explaining, or arguing about in Korean. We did that,
      over and over, for years.
    </p>

    <p>
      Building those houses taught us the other half of the job. We renovated
      them ourselves — working side by side with the wallpaper crews, flooring
      installers, carpenters, and electricians who actually keep Seoul's homes
      running. That's where our network of tradespeople comes from: not a
      directory, but people we've stood next to on real jobs. And it's where
      we learned exactly how much of this world runs on Korean phone calls,
      Korean apps, and knowing who to ask — which is precisely the part
      that's closed to you if you don't speak the language. Balli Balli Seoul
      is that access, opened up.
    </p>

    <h2>How it works</h2>

    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Message us on <a href={WHATSAPP_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">WhatsApp</a></strong>
        — in English, with photos of the problem. First answer is free.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>We diagnose and quote.</strong> We tell you what it is, what
        it should cost, and what the options are. The price is confirmed with
        you in the chat before any work starts.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>We handle it.</strong> Depending on the job, we either take
        care of it ourselves or send a specialist from our network who's good
        at exactly that work — while we stay in the middle, in English, from
        start to finish.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <p>
      And it's not only repairs. If what you need is an errand — something
      bought, filed, picked up, or sorted out in Korean — we
      <a href="/etc">do that too</a>.
    </p>

    <p>
      Our fee is built into the price we confirm with you — kept at a
      reasonable level, agreed before work starts, with no surprises after.
    </p>

    <h2>The company</h2>

    <p>
      Balli Balli Seoul is operated by <strong>Jiinus (지인어스)</strong>, a
      registered Korean business.
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>Representative: Yeonbum Kim</li>
      <li>Business registration: 108-24-44405</li>
      <li>E-commerce registration: 2025-서울중구-143</li>
      <li>Service area: Seoul</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      As a booking and coordination service, we connect you with independent
      local providers and confirm all terms with you before work begins — the
      full notice is in the footer of every page.
    </p>

    <aside class="cta">
      <p>
        <strong>Something broken, confusing, or stuck in Korean?</strong>
        Send us a photo — we'll tell you what it is and what it should cost,
        in English. First answer is free.
      </p>
      <a href={WHATSAPP_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="cta-btn">💬 WhatsApp Us — in English</a>
    </aside>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  h1{font-size:clamp(26px,4.6vw,40px);line-height:1.15;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.02em;margin-bottom:24px}
  h2{font-size:24px;font-weight:800;margin:36px 0 12px;letter-spacing:-.01em}
  .about p{margin:14px 0}
  .about ol,.about ul{margin:14px 0;padding-left:26px}
  .about li{margin:8px 0}
  .about a{color:var(--primary-dark);font-weight:600;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px}
  .cta{background:var(--primary-light);border:2px solid #bbf7d0;border-radius:var(--radius);padding:22px;margin-top:44px;font-size:15px}
  .cta-btn{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;margin-top:14px;background:var(--whatsapp);color:#fff !important;font-weight:800;padding:13px 24px;border-radius:999px;text-decoration:none !important}
  .cta-btn:hover{filter:brightness(.95)}
</style>
